  "assessment": "Reviewed every exact-target interest: twelve direct interests, twenty-nine curricular topics, six illustrations and twelve outcomes. Dutch structure and language change require explicit limits; beginner Dutch, stylistics and rhetoric offer practical and analytical overlap. Dutch literature, literary interpretation, narrative and cultural history substantiate the literature option. Language in society and contemporary society support the public-debate direction, with rhetoric, public argument and media as programme-grounded methods. Particular projects, jobs and further qualifications remain search-only and do not drive selection.",
